{"id": "sllama0024", "pool": "sllama", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2364531889, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "41a5db294317f43671e96d4157e9209f1111c47f4a217fdcbe5e389282f03cfe", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "How many words are in the Shema prayer? ", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/sllama0024.wav", "input_sha256": "3b46c5dcf9c915cf8015acde838477636959e924977a131b94d3706b8cd2cb7e", "input_samples": 38334, "input_s": 2.396, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.6482, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "It depends what you mean by “the Shema prayer”: First verse only (“Shema Yisrael…”): 6 Hebrew words. , Full Shema — the three biblical paragraphs recited in Jewish prayer: traditionally 245 Hebrew words. , In synagogue practice, 3 words are added/repeated (“Adonai Eloheichem Emet”) to bring the total to 248 words, corresponding to the traditional count of 248 limbs/organs.", "expert_answer": "It depends what you mean by **“the Shema prayer”**:\n\n- **First verse only** (“Shema Yisrael…”): **6 Hebrew words**.\n- **Full Shema** — the three biblical paragraphs recited in Jewish prayer: traditionally **245 Hebrew words**.\n- In synagogue practice, **3 words** are added/repeated (“Adonai Eloheichem Emet”) to bring the total to **248 words**, corresponding to the traditional count of 248 limbs/organs.", "transcript": "How many words are in the Shema prayer?\n", "asr_s": 0.65, "expert_s": 3.93, "expert_input_samples": 38334, "expert_input_s": 2.396, "expert_input_sha256": "3b46c5dcf9c915cf8015acde838477636959e924977a131b94d3706b8cd2cb7e", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.012, "relay_synth_ms": 16341, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "a